  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Green Economy Programme in the Philippines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Context: The proposed intervention will support the Philippines&#xbf; transition towards a circular economy and to pursue an inclusive and green recovery by unlocking the potential, the delivery and the operationalisation of the circular economy and by promoting and implementing climate change mitigation measures. The intervention will take three levels:(i) establishing a central-Government level Policy Dialogue Platform mobilising EU expertise to facilitate policy formulation, improve city to city collaboration through supporting the development of a National Circular Economy Strategy and Roadmap, and to apply the dialogue&#xbf;s outcomes (linked to Specific Objective 1 of the action);(ii) working with Local government units (LGUs) where the EU expertise will support to define and implement human rights and gender-responsive policies on circular economy and climate change, outreach and support of local business and civil society, including support to less advanced LGUs (linked to Specific Objective 2 of the action); and(iii) enhancing engagement of the private and financial sectors into the circular waste economy (linked to Specific Objective 3 of the action).(iv) working with national and local government and private sector stakeholders to increase energy efficiency and renewable energy deployment to support climate change mitigation (linked to Specific Objective 4 of the action).</narrative>
  </description>
